   "path": "sections.story.1.en",
   "before": "Grant was explicit that he did not know what Lee was feeling. Lee was a man of much dignity with an impassible face; it was impossible to say whether he was inwardly glad the end had finally come, or sad at the result and too manly to show it. Whatever his feelings, they were entirely concealed from Grant's observation. Grant's own were a different matter: jubilant on receipt of the letter, he now found them sad and depressed.",
   "after": "Grant was explicit that he did not know what Lee was feeling. In Grant's description, Lee was a man of much dignity with an impassible face; it was impossible to say whether he was inwardly glad the end had finally come, or sad at the result and too manly to show it. Whatever his feelings, they were entirely concealed from Grant's observation. Grant's own were a different matter: jubilant on receipt of the letter, he now found them sad and depressed.",
